{
 "thread": "p20uDv4hOuE",
 "subject": "How is the variance in \"points.var\" of gpagen calculated?",
 "messages_listed": 3,
 "last_activity": "2017-09-14T14:33:02Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "PocYGLH4CwAJ",
   "from": "Peter Vermeiren",
   "author": "019a7a198af7eab6",
   "date": "2017-09-14T08:36:40Z",
   "subject": "How is the variance in \"points.var\" of gpagen calculated?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Calibri\" size=\"3\">How is the\r\nvariance among landmark points calculated after Procrustes superposition using\r\nthe function gpagen. In other words where do the values in the component\r\n“point.var” in the gpagen object come from.</font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Calibri\" size=\"3\">I conducted\r\na Procrustes superposition (gpagen) on the example plethodon landmark data of\r\nthe package (looking only at the landmarks of the Jord species).</font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Calibri\" size=\"3\">I then\r\ncompared the output of the “points.var” with a calculation of the standard\r\ndeviation for all 12 landmarks in the x direction among all 20 species, and the\r\nsame for the y direction. These numbers are not the same, hence the variance\r\ndepicted in “points.var” is not the standard deviation or standard error. So,\r\nmy question is, what is it. </font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Calibri\" size=\"3\">Big thanks\r\nfor any insights. Below is my code:</font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Calibri\" size=\"3\"># the data</font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Calibri\" size=\"3\">data(plethodon)</font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font size=\"3\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Calibri\">Res &lt;-\r\nplethodon$land<span>       </span></font></font></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Calibri\" size=\"3\">index &lt;-\r\nwhich(dimnames(Res)[[3]] ==&quot;Jord&quot;) </font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Calibri\" size=\"3\">Res.jord\r\n&lt;- Res[,,index]</font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font size=\"3\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Calibri\">#\r\nProcrustes analysis<span>                    </span></font></font></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font size=\"3\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Calibri\">PA &lt;-\r\ngpagen(Res.jord)<span>      </span></font></font></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\"><font size=\"3\"><font color=\"#000000\">PA$points.var<span>       </span></font></font><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\"># variance coming from the GPA</font></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Calibri\" size=\"3\"># my own\r\ncalculation of variation</font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"FR-CH\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Calibri\" size=\"3\">Sd.x &lt;-\r\nNULL</font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Calibri\" size=\"3\">Sd.y &lt;-\r\nNULL</font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font size=\"3\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Calibri\">for (l in\r\n1:dim(Res)[1]){<span>   </span></font></font></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\"><font size=\"3\"><font color=\"#000000\">Sd.x<span>    </span></font></font><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\">&lt;- c(Sd.x, sd(PA$coords [l, 1,])) </font></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\"><span><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\"> </font></span><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\">Sd.y</font><span><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\">   \r\n</font></span><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\">&lt;- c(Sd.y, sd(PA$coords [l, 2,]))</font></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font size=\"3\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Calibri\">}<span>  </span></font></font></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\"><font size=\"3\"><font color=\"#000000\">cbind(Sd.x,\r\nSd.y)<span>  </span></font></font><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\"># the variance I calculated, not\r\nthe same.</font><span><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\">     </font></span></font></span></p></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "mUOB8nj5CwAJ",
   "from": "Mike Collyer",
   "author": "aab55242ff4da6c6",
