   "subject": "Re: [geomorph-r-package] How is the variance in \"points.var\" of gpagen calculated?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">Standard deviation is the square root of variance.  <div><br></div><div>The $pt.var calculation uses population variance (divided by n), not sample variance (divided by n - 1), as it references the population of configurations in GPA and not a sample of them.  Your use of sd assumes they are a sample.  Finally, the calculation does not re-center the values, as they have already been centered by subtracting the consensus configuration.  The sd function will assume they have not been centered and will center them.  This should have no effect but could lead to rounding error differences.</div><div><br></div><div>Mike</div><div><br><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On Sep 14, 2017, at 4:36 AM, Peter Vermeiren &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">peter.v...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\" size=\"3\">How is the\r\nvariance among landmark points calculated after Procrustes superposition using\r\nthe function gpagen. In other words where do the values in the component\r\n“point.var” in the gpagen object come from.</font></span></p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\" size=\"3\">I conducted\r\na Procrustes superposition (gpagen) on the example plethodon landmark data of\r\nthe package (looking only at the landmarks of the Jord species).</font></span></p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\" size=\"3\">I then\r\ncompared the output of the “points.var” with a calculation of the standard\r\ndeviation for all 12 landmarks in the x direction among all 20 species, and the\r\nsame for the y direction. These numbers are not the same, hence the variance\r\ndepicted in “points.var” is not the standard deviation or standard error. So,\r\nmy question is, what is it. </font></span></p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\" size=\"3\">Big thanks\r\nfor any insights. Below is my code:</font></span></p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\" size=\"3\"># the data</font></span></p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\" size=\"3\">data(plethodon)</font></span></p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font size=\"3\"><font><font face=\"Calibri\">Res &lt;-\r\nplethodon$land<span>       </span></font></font></font></span></p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\" size=\"3\">index &lt;-\r\nwhich(dimnames(Res)[[3]] ==&quot;Jord&quot;) </font></span></p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\" size=\"3\">Res.jord\r\n&lt;- Res[,,index]</font></span></p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font size=\"3\"><font><font face=\"Calibri\">#\r\nProcrustes analysis<span>                    </span></font></font></font></span></p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font size=\"3\"><font><font face=\"Calibri\">PA &lt;-\r\ngpagen(Res.jord)<span>      </span></font></font></font></span></p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\"><font size=\"3\"><font>PA$points.var<span>       </span></font></font><font size=\"3\"># variance coming from the GPA</font></font></span></p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\" size=\"3\"># my own\r\ncalculation of variation</font></span></p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"FR-CH\"><font face=\"Calibri\" size=\"3\">Sd.x &lt;-\r\nNULL</font></span></p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\" size=\"3\">Sd.y &lt;-\r\nNULL</font></span></p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font size=\"3\"><font><font face=\"Calibri\">for (l in\r\n1:dim(Res)[1]){<span>   </span></font></font></font></span></p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\"><font size=\"3\"><font>Sd.x<span>    </span></font></font><font size=\"3\">&lt;- c(Sd.x, sd(PA$coords [l, 1,])) </font></font></span></p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\"><span><font size=\"3\"> </font></span><font size=\"3\">Sd.y</font><span><font size=\"3\">   \r\n</font></span><font size=\"3\">&lt;- c(Sd.y, sd(PA$coords [l, 2,]))</font></font></span></p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font size=\"3\"><font><font face=\"Calibri\">}<span>  </span></font></font></font></span></p><font face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\"><font size=\"3\"><font>cbind(Sd.x,\r\nSd.y)<span>  </span></font></font><font size=\"3\"># the variance I calculated, not\r\nthe same.</font><span><font size=\"3\">     </font></span></font></span></p></div><div><br></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
